IMPORTANT POINTS

    - SVM is a supervised machine learning algorithm
    - It is mainly used for classification
    - It tries to maximize the margin between classes
    - Support vectors determine the decision boundary
    - It can use different kernels for linear and nonlinear classification
    - Feature scaling is important for SVM
    - C controls the trade-off between margin size and classification errors

